# Peka — Co-op 2D Platform Puzzler

> Game Design Document (living draft). Filled out as we ideate.
>
> **Decided:** symmetric players + co-op verbs · local couch · mysterious/eerie tone · lightless caverns · **mirrored-gravity core mechanic**

---

## 1. Description

A **2D co-op platform game** built around **cooperative puzzles**. Two players
travel together through **one long level** in a system of **lightless caverns**.
Each player is bound to an **opposite gravity** — one walks the floor, one walks
the ceiling — sharing the same tunnel from mirrored sides. The level is designed
so it is **impossible to complete solo**: clearing it means each player solving
the *other's* path.

Tone is **mysterious and eerie** — sparse, atmospheric, told through the
environment rather than text (Limbo / Inside lineage). Two small, vulnerable
figures; a large, unexplained dark.

**Core pillars**
- **Forced cooperation** — no section clears without two players.
- **Mirrored gravity** — opposite-surface play is the signature verb (see §2).
- **Puzzle-first platforming** — movement is the verb; the brain-teaser is the challenge.
- **One handcrafted journey** — a single, long, escalating level.
- **Wordless atmosphere** — eerie mood, environmental storytelling, minimal UI.

---

## 2. Cooperation Model — ✅ Symmetric + ✅ Mirrored Gravity

Both players control **identical** characters. The dependency comes from each
being bound to **opposite gravity**: Player A falls "down," Player B falls "up,"
so they live on opposite surfaces of the same space. Neither can clear a section
alone — your hazards are on your partner's surface and vice versa.

Symmetry holds: same controls, same abilities, only orientation differs.

### ⭐ Core mechanic: mirrored gravity — _key open decisions_
- [ ] **Fixed vs. toggleable** — are roles fixed (A=floor, B=ceiling all game), or
      can a player flip their own gravity (at will / only in flip-zones)? **(biggest lever)**
- [ ] **Spatial model** — shared tunnel (ceiling has its own real geometry, both
      in one continuous space) vs. mirrored/reflected worlds. _(lean: shared tunnel)_
- [ ] **Falling off your surface** — death, or you fall across to your partner's gravity?

### Cooperative verbs (the teamwork vocabulary) — _draft, gated on above_
- **Clear the other's path** — your lever opens your partner's gate; your block buries your partner's hazard.
- **Mid-platforms** — platforms both can use from opposite sides (one on top, one underneath).
- **Drop across the divide** — objects obey local gravity; pass items via flip-zones or neutral pockets.
- **Counter-position** — shield your partner from a shadow creature pinned to your surface.
- **Gravity flip-zones** — tiles that swap a player's surface to meet, cross, or reposition.

- [ ] Lock the final ~4–6 verbs once fixed-vs-toggle is decided

